<!--
READ 1000 — Women's Sphere  (Activity bank)

The Women's Sphere form of the READ 1000 module. It carries the structure and
interface the parallel form has over its own texts — the American Yawp chapter
(Ch. 11, "The Cotton Revolution" — women, the family, and the "cult of
domesticity"), a period image ("The Sphere of Woman," Godey's Lady's Book,
1850), a magazine article ("The Unglamorous Truth About the Average Tradwife,"
The Atlantic, 2026) — and its own set of assessment items. One deliberate
departure, in both forms:
  * "Joe's notes" (the note-checking matrix) tests the TEXTBOOK excerpt.

Layout (see temperance_b_full_sba_part1.olx). The tab strip is the top level;
its first tab, "Discussion," is the session itself:
  * Left  pane : the scripted small-group conversation
                 (temperance_b_full_dialogue_part1.chatpeg). Peers Danielle,
                 Joe, and Karis and the reading instructor Professor Booker.
  * Right pane : a UseHistory (tmb_main) the conversation drives via target
                 embeds (and, for parking the pane empty, `tmb_main <- tmb_blank`).
Each READING screen below — the lecture, the four textbook parts, the
engraving — also gets its own tab, via <Use ref="..."> of the same block, so a
student can reopen it (with their own highlights) at any point.

The textbook is CHUNKED across four Main Content readings (tmb_tb_a/a2/b/c),
one per paragraph (para 4 folds in the short Southern-women paragraph), so peer
dialogue can mediate each passage before the next appears and before the items
that depend on it.
This FULL build carries the module through all five parts: textbook, image,
article, a then/now synthesis, and Pulling It Together — the culminating
four-or-five-sentence synthesis.

Ids are prefixed `tmb_` and the namespace is `womens_sphere`, so this form's
ids never collide with the parallel form's.
     -->

