<TabularMCQGrader id="tmb_notecheck_grader">
<TabularMCQ id="tmb_notecheck_grid">
cols:
  - Correct and central to the text
  - Correct but less important
  - Not correct
rows:
  - "The 'cult of domesticity' held that a woman's proper place was the home, as guardian of virtue and morality.|n_ideal[Correct and central to the text]"
  - "Women took the very ideology that kept them at home and used it to fashion a new public role for themselves.|n_public[Correct and central to the text]"
  - "The Second Great Awakening and new education for girls helped middle-class women leave home to join reform societies.|n_awakening[Correct and central to the text]"
  - "These ideas about womanhood applied mainly to upper- and middle-class women, not working-class women.|n_class[Correct but less important]"
  - "Southern women were more often told to be a calming, moralizing influence at home than to organize reform societies.|n_south[Correct but less important]"
  - "The cult of domesticity was invented by factory owners to force women to take jobs in factories.|n_factory[Not correct]"
</TabularMCQ>
</TabularMCQGrader>
</CapaProblem> <!-- tmb_notecheck_problem -->
