<Vertical id="tmb_q_domestic_screen">
<CapaProblem id="tmb_q_domestic_problem" title="Vocabulary: domestic" maxAttempts="1">
<KeyGrader id="tmb_q_domestic_grader">
<ChoiceInput id="tmb_q_domestic">
<Markdown>
Choose the best definition for **domestic** as it's used here:

> "They were to be pious, pure, submissive, and **domestic**."
</Markdown>
  <Distractor value="made_in_country" > Made or produced inside one's own country.        </Distractor>
         <Key value="home_focused"    > Devoted to the home and family life.               </Key>
  <Distractor value="tame_animal"     > Tame or trained, like a household animal.         </Distractor>
  <Distractor value="strict_rules"    > Strict and demanding about rules.                 </Distractor>
</ChoiceInput>
</KeyGrader>

<!-- Karis names the morphology link in the dialogue after this: "domestic"
   (adjective) shares a root with "domesticity" (noun) from part 2. -->
<Markdown when="@tmb_q_domestic.value === 'made_in_country' &amp;&amp; @tmb_q_domestic_problem.submitCount &gt; 0">
*A real sense of "domestic" (as in "domestic products"), but not this one. Here it's about the home: devoted to home and family life.*
</Markdown>
<Markdown when="@tmb_q_domestic.value === 'tame_animal' &amp;&amp; @tmb_q_domestic_problem.submitCount &gt; 0">
*Also a real sense ("a domestic animal"), but the sentence is describing a woman, not a pet. Here it means devoted to the home and family.*
</Markdown>
<Markdown when="@tmb_q_domestic.value === 'strict_rules' &amp;&amp; @tmb_q_domestic_problem.submitCount &gt; 0">
*Nothing in "domestic" is about strictness. It's about the home — devoted to home and family life.*
</Markdown>
<Markdown when="@tmb_q_domestic.value === 'home_focused' &amp;&amp; @tmb_q_domestic_problem.submitCount &gt; 0">
*Right — devoted to the home and family. It's the same root you saw in "domesticity" back in part 2 — the noun for the whole idea.*
</Markdown>
</CapaProblem> <!-- tmb_q_domestic_problem -->
</Vertical> <!-- tmb_q_domestic_screen -->


